<p>Interestingly, the ablation study showed that applying FKL over all tokens (**Full FKL**) completely collapsed training, yielding only 1.40% average accuracy. This confirms the paper's insight: top-k FKL is a biased approximation of the full vocabulary distribution, and applying it globally introduces corrupted gradients. It is only when targeted selectively at outlier tokens that FKL acts as an optimization anchor.</p>
</section>

